Subject: [PATCH] test(kanban): fence denied-claim disposition races [daveey]

Problem: hub claims could follow a negative admission verdict without an explicit
keep. Historical census since 1794634561: 23 claims, 10 latest prior denies;
8 already carried older keep reasons and 2 lacked keep/force. These are baseline,
not postinstall measurements. Eleven no-verdict claims were explicitly pinned
cards outside the unlabelled legacy/previously-denied-pin claim-screen scope.

Why (creation): pool_route retained home-coordination cards because the worker
pickup gate cannot execute those actions, but only wrote home, not kept.
Why (claim): any prior verdict skipped judging; denied_target waited 300 seconds
and silently skipped structural/home keeps, letting a young deny be claimed.
The screen also excluded the exact machine:hub pin used by a bounced deny.
Why (coordination): model portability and deterministic execution capability had
no common recorded final disposition. Bare home coordination uses local custody;
a model judgment cannot grant a worker that authority. Creation and claim now
honor the same pickup constraint and record the keep, avoiding bounce loops.
Root (happened): verdict presence was treated as execution permission, instead
of requiring admitted, structurally kept, or moved before claim. Exception and
judge-outage paths also returned permission; now unresolved candidates defer.
Root (not caught): unjudged_claims excluded every earlier verdict, even denies.
Recurrence: the prior admission rollout watch (#1637/#1810/#1811/#1911/#2881)
checked absence of judgment, not denied execution. The chronological detector
now includes denied-without-keep and creation-payload fallback.

Countermeasures and proof:
- Five initial regression failures before production changes; additional RED
  denied-pin, keep-churn, missing-queue, doctor and exception/outage cases.
- Final consumer snapshot fb55360a: 13 files, 356 passed, zero failed, rc=0.
- Added actual dispatch race controls: mutate event head during move/keep
  decision; neither path claims or records a stale disposition. Exact own pin,
  other pin, admit, absent verdict and forced controls retain scoped behavior.
- This test file: 26 passed, zero failed, rc=0, including quiet no-queue deferral.
- Read-only eligibility replay across 22 hub board/shadow databases, 24947 rows:
  zero currently-ready changes; next-ready simulation changes two replicas of
  the original bounced machine:hub denial, both inspected intended matches.
- Private corpus stays off GitHub. Required CI and independent exact-head review
  remain mandatory; installation and the requested 24-hour census follow land.
